{#- Listen2 2.0 draft: "Hear it". One paragraph full of the hard parts, read at three paces by one voice and by
    three voices. The other-engines row is built but off (hearIt.showOtherEngines): the fact sheet says we have
    tested no other product and must not imply a comparison. Plan section 4. -#}
{% from "components/listen2-2/slots.njk" import audioSlot %}
{%- set h = listen2Voices.hearIt -%}
{%- set dir = listen2Voices.voiceDir -%}
    <!-- Hear it -->
    <section id="hear-it" style="max-width: 1200px; margin: 0 auto; padding: 88px 24px; display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 40px" aria-labelledby="l2-hear">
      <div style="max-width: 760px; display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 16px">
        <div style="font-family: 'Atkinson Hyperlegible Mono', monospace; font-size: 13px; letter-spacing: 0.08em; text-transform: uppercase; color: #FF66C4">Hear it</div>
        <h2 id="l2-hear" style="margin: 0; font-size: clamp(32px, 4vw, 48px); line-height: 1.1; font-weight: 700; letter-spacing: -0.02em">Listen to the hard parts</h2>
        <p style="margin: 0; font-size: 19px; line-height: 1.6; color: #D4D4D0">Any voice sounds fine on a line of poetry. Real documents are full of harder things: a time, a price, an initialism, a word whose sound depends on what it means. This paragraph has all of them. Read it, then hear what the Listen2 Voices do with it.</p>
      </div>
      <div style="display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; gap: 40px; align-items: flex-start">
        <figure style="flex: 1 1 420px; min-width: 0; margin: 0; border: 1px solid #2A2A2D; border-radius: 24px; background: #131315; padding: clamp(24px, 3vw, 36px); display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 14px">
          <figcaption style="font-family: 'Atkinson Hyperlegible Mono', monospace; font-size: 13px; letter-spacing: 0.08em; text-transform: uppercase; color: #A3A3A0">The paragraph</figcaption>
          {%- set parts = h.passage.split(" " + h.highlightWord + " ") %}
          <p style="margin: 0; font-size: 21px; line-height: 1.5; color: #F5F5F2">{% if parts.length > 1 %}{{ parts[0] }} <span class="l2-hl">{{ h.highlightWord }}</span> {{ parts.slice(1).join(" " + h.highlightWord + " ") }}{% else %}{{ h.passage }}{% endif %}</p>
        </figure>
        <div style="flex: 1 1 420px; min-width: 0; display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 32px">
          <div style="display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 14px">
            <h3 style="margin: 0; font-size: 22px; font-weight: 700">One voice, three paces</h3>
            <p style="margin: 0; font-size: 16px; line-height: 1.55; color: #A3A3A0">Pace changes how fast the voice reads, not who it sounds like. Here is {{ h.paceVoice }} at the slowest step, at Normal and at the fastest step.</p>
            <div style="display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fill, minmax(180px, 1fr)); gap: 14px">
              {%- for s in h.pace %}
              {{ audioSlot("Pace " + s.label, dir + s.file, s.ready) }}
              {%- endfor %}
            </div>
          </div>
          <div style="display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 14px">
            <h3 style="margin: 0; font-size: 22px; font-weight: 700">Three voices, one paragraph</h3>
            <div style="display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fill, minmax(180px, 1fr)); gap: 14px">
              {%- for s in h.voices %}
              {{ audioSlot(s.label, dir + s.file, s.ready) }}
              {%- endfor %}
            </div>
          </div>
          {%- if h.showOtherEngines %}
          <div style="display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 14px">
            <h3 style="margin: 0; font-size: 22px; font-weight: 700">The same paragraph from each kind of voice in Listen2</h3>
            <p style="margin: 0; font-size: 16px; line-height: 1.55; color: #A3A3A0">Listen2 has more than one kind of voice, and people like different ones. Here is the paragraph from each.</p>
            <div style="display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fill, minmax(180px, 1fr)); gap: 14px">
              {%- for s in h.otherEngines %}
              {{ audioSlot(s.label, dir + s.file, s.ready) }}
              {%- endfor %}
            </div>
          </div>
          {%- endif %}
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>
